@startuml agent-builder-phase4-flow
' ============================================================================
'  AGENT BUILDER - PHASE 4 (freeze create_agent)
'  Where the hand-off happens during one "build me an agent" turn.
'  Read the ACT brackets; the notes on the right explain in plain english.
'  Render (from this folder):
'    java -jar ../../../../plantuml.jar -tpng agent-builder-phase4-flow.puml
' ============================================================================

skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam ArrowFontColor #444444
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #6A6A6A
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF4E5
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #C9A227
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFFDF0
skinparam NoteBorderColor #C9B458
skinparam NoteFontSize 12
skinparam partitionBorderColor #9AA0B5
skinparam partitionFontStyle bold
skinparam partitionFontSize 13

title Agent Builder - PHASE 4: the hand-off\ncreate_agent lays the foundation, then gets out of the way

start

group ACT 1 . SCAFFOLD  (create_agent - the only part with code)
  partition "the model creates the agent  <<MODIFIED>>" #FFE0B2 {
    :model calls **create_agent**{id, name, identity, ...}\n<color:#1B5E20>+ version  <<NEW param>></color>;
    :write agent.toml SKELETON\nname, version, description, model, heartbeat,\n[capabilities], [subagents];
    :write IDENTITY.md (+ AGENTS.md, HEARTBEAT.md if given);
    :**registry.add(id)** -> the agent is LIVE right now;
    :<color:#1B5E20>return a HAND-OFF, not just "created":</color>\n<color:#1B5E20>what was written | what is still missing |</color>\n<color:#1B5E20>call write for [app]/ui/tools, then validate_agent</color>;
  }
  note right
    **PLAIN ENGLISH**
    Why keep this tool at all, if the model can just write files?

    Three things `write` cannot do:
      * guarantee VALID TOML key order - every top-level key must
        come before the first [table], or it silently lands inside
        that table (this is the purple-dot bug's root cause)
      * refuse to overwrite 'main'
      * **register the agent LIVE** - after this call the agent is
        resolvable on the very next message, with no restart

    So it keeps the skeleton. It does not keep the rest.
  end note
end group

group ACT 2 . THE FREEZE  (the actual decision of this phase)
  if (does the user want [app], ui/, tool wiring, display keys?) then (yes - the usual case)
    partition "everything else is plain file writing" #EDE7F6 {
      :model calls **write** for each of them\n[app] table | tagline/color/suggestions | [tools]\n[plugins.<p>.tools.<t>] | ui/* | templates/*;
      :model calls **create_skill** for playbooks;
      :model calls **create_tool**(agent=<id>) for private tools;
    }
    note right
      **PLAIN ENGLISH - why create_agent does NOT grow parameters**

      The remaining half of agent.toml has no fixed shape. The
      big one is:

          [plugins.<plugin>.tools.<tool>]

      any plugin x any tool x any setting. figure-creator's entire
      engine lives there - which image model, which template, what
      resolution, which vision model for reading labels.

      You cannot turn "any plugin x any tool x any knob" into a
      list of tool parameters. So a parameterised create_agent can
      never be finished - it would grow forever and still be
      incomplete.

      Meanwhile the model already writes TOML perfectly well, and
      since phase 1 it has the full grammar in build-agent/SKILL.md.
      So: let it write. That is the freeze.
    end note
  else (no - a plain chat agent)
    :the skeleton alone is already a working agent;
  endif
end group

group ACT 3 . SAFETY NET  (phase 3 makes the freeze safe)
  partition "check what was written" #C8E6C9 {
    :model calls **validate_agent**{agent_id};
    if (findings?) then (yes)
      :fix with `write`, validate again;
      detach
    else (clean)
    endif
  }
  note right
    **PLAIN ENGLISH**
    Freezing create_agent only works because something ELSE
    catches mistakes. That is phase 3.

    Without validate_agent, "just write the TOML yourself"
    would be a way to ship silent bugs. With it, a mistake
    comes straight back with the file, the reason, and the fix -
    and the model repairs it before you ever see the agent.

    Phase 3 is what earns phase 4.
  end note

  partition "make edits take effect" #C8E6C9 {
    :model calls **reload_agent**{agent_id}\n(agent.toml changed after create_agent registered it);
  }
end group

group ACT 4 . DONE
  partition "the user tries it" #E0F2F1 {
    :new chat with the agent, or its app window;
  }
  note right
    **THE DIVISION OF LABOUR, IN ONE LINE**
      create_agent  -> the skeleton + making it live
      write         -> the open-ended rest
      create_skill  -> playbooks
      create_tool   -> private tools
      validate      -> catches what write got wrong
      reload        -> makes it real
  end note
}

stop

legend left
  | Colour | Meaning |
  |<#FFE0B2> | **MODIFIED in phase 4** - CreateAgentTool (one file) |
  |<#C8E6C9> | phase 3 - the safety net that makes the freeze viable |
  |<#EDE7F6> | existing - `write` / create_skill / create_tool |
  |<#E0F2F1> | outcome |
endlegend

@enduml
